problems.problem:
Sofia and Viktor play the following game on a $2022 \times 2022$ board:

First, Sofia completely covers the board with dominoes that do not overlap and do not go outside the board;

Next, Viktor writes a positive integer $n$ on a sheet of paper, without seeing the specific configuration of the dominoes on the board;

Then Viktor looks at the board with the dominoes on it, chooses $n$ of them and fixes (glues) them to the board;

After that, Sofia removes the remaining (unglued) dominoes from the board and tries to obtain a new complete covering of the board which differs from the initial one.

If Sofia succeeds, she wins; otherwise Viktor is the winner.

Find the smallest possible value of $n$ for which Viktor can always win, regardless of the initial configuration.
